        "description": "<p>Let\u2019s take a pair of two types <code>&lt;YourType, bool&gt;</code> - what can you do with such composition?</p>\n<p>In this article, I\u2019ll describe <code>std::optional</code> - a helper &ldquo;vocabulary&rdquo; type added in C++17. It\u2019s a wrapper that either contains a value of your type or is empty. Let\u2019s see where it can be useful and how you can use it.</p>\n<blockquote class=\"hint note\">\n\n  Updated in September 2026 with C++20, C++23, and C++26 changes.\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"intro\">\nIntro \n  \n<a class=\"hash-link\" href=\"#intro\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<svg class=\"fill-current o-60 hover-accent-color-light\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"22\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 0h24v24H0z\" fill=\"none\"></path><path d=\"M3.9 12c0-1.71 1.39-3.1 3.1-3.1h4V7H7c-2.76.0-5 2.24-5 5s2.24 5 5 5h4v-1.9H7c-1.71.0-3.1-1.39-3.1-3.1zM8 13h8v-2H8v2zm9-6h-4v1.9h4c1.71.0 3.1 1.39 3.1 3.1s-1.39 3.1-3.1 3.1h-4V17h4c2.76.0 5-2.24 5-5s-2.24-5-5-5z\"></path></svg>\n    </a>&n",
